# Java 21 / Spring Boot 3

Steering only: follow these conventions when generating or editing backend code. Do not implement application features from this rule alone.

## Language (Java 21)

- Use **records**, **sealed classes/interfaces**, and **pattern matching** (`switch` / `instanceof`).
- Prefer immutable types over mutable beans. Do not use Lombok `@Data` when a record or sealed hierarchy is enough.

```java
// ❌ BAD
@Data public class TicketDto { private String id; private String status; }

// ✅ GOOD
public record TicketResponse(String id, TicketStatus status) {}

public sealed interface TicketCommand permits CreateTicket, ChangeStatus {}
```

## Layered architecture

Order of dependency: **Controller → Service → Repository → Domain**.

| Layer | Allowed | Forbidden |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Controller | HTTP mapping, `@Valid`, status codes, map records | Business rules, JPA, entities as JSON |
| Service | Use cases, `@Transactional`, domain invariants | `HttpServletRequest`, status codes, SQL |
| Repository | Spring Data JPA interfaces | HTTP, DTO mapping, business rules |
| Domain | Entities, value objects, status enums | Framework types leaking to API |

Package by feature (`ticket/`, …) with these layers inside each feature. Constructor injection only.

## Immutable DTOs

- Request and response types are **Java records**.
- Never return JPA entities from controllers.
- Bean Validation on request records (`@Valid`, `@NotBlank`, `@Size`, …).

## Errors

- Map exceptions to **RFC 7807** `ProblemDetail` (`application/problem+json`) via `@ControllerAdvice`.
- Do not return `{ "message": "..." }` or leak stack traces.

## Persistence

- **Spring Data JPA** + **PostgreSQL** for runtime / non-local profiles.
- **H2** for tests and a local/dev profile only.
- No hardcoded credentials; env / Spring config only.
